{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"pop56-group-1","type":"group","x":0,"y":240,"width":2560,"height":520,"label":"1 · 先分清人口量、人口事件与生育强度","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-group-2","type":"group","x":0,"y":840,"width":2560,"height":550,"label":"2 · 收入改善为什么可能被人口反馈吸收","color":"6"},
		{"id":"pop56-group-3","type":"group","x":0,"y":1470,"width":2560,"height":520,"label":"3 · 家庭为什么调整子女数量与教育投入","color":"2"},
		{"id":"pop56-group-4","type":"group","x":0,"y":2070,"width":2560,"height":400,"label":"4 · 从家庭选择到人口转型：还要看年龄结构","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-group-5","type":"group","x":0,"y":2550,"width":2560,"height":520,"label":"5 · 年龄窗口怎样才会变成人均产出","color":"4"},
		{"id":"pop56-group-6","type":"group","x":0,"y":3150,"width":2560,"height":1140,"label":"6 · 老龄化以后：谁生产、谁消费、谁筹资","color":"3"},
		{"id":"pop56-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":2560,"height":180,"text":"# 人口、家庭选择与增长转型\n\n连续阅读：[[02_Economy/10_发展经济学/09_人口、家庭选择与增长转型|课程笔记]]。按编号向下读，各区内比较相邻卡片；点击短标题进入共享原子。颜色区分问题领域，不表示掌握程度。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRead the numbered sections from top to bottom. Open a short title for its shared atom; colour marks the question being studied, not mastery.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"pop56-011","type":"text","x":40,"y":290,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[粗出生率]]\n\n出生数 ÷ 总人口暴露；不是每位女性的生育强度。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nBirths per total population exposure, not fertility per woman.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-010","type":"text","x":720,"y":290,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[人口变动恒等式]]\n\n人口增量 = 出生 − 死亡 + 净迁入；先统一地域、时期与人口口径。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPopulation change equals births minus deaths plus net immigration, on a consistent basis.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-012","type":"text","x":1400,"y":290,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[粗死亡率]]\n\n死亡数 ÷ 总人口暴露；年龄构成改变也能使它上升。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDeaths per total population exposure can rise because the population is older.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-013","type":"text","x":2080,"y":290,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[总和生育率]]\n\n按当期年龄别生育率合成的终身生育量；不同于[[粗出生率|全人口出生频率]]。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA synthetic lifetime measure based on current age-specific fertility rates.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-measure-bridge","type":"text","x":40,"y":620,"width":2480,"height":110,"text":"同一人口暴露下：粗出生率 − 粗死亡率描述自然增长；总人口增长还要计入净迁移。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOn the same exposure basis, CBR minus CDR measures natural increase; total growth also includes net migration.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"pop56-001","type":"text","x":40,"y":890,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[马尔萨斯陷阱]]\n\n收入改善引起人口反馈，资源约束使人均改善难以持续。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPopulation feedback can absorb income gains when resources are constrained.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"6"},
		{"id":"pop56-002","type":"text","x":720,"y":890,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[马尔萨斯生存收入]]\n\n给定人口行为和死亡条件下，使人口净增长为零的收入阈值。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe income threshold for zero net population growth under a specified demographic schedule.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"6"},
		{"id":"pop56-003","type":"text","x":1400,"y":890,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[马尔萨斯技术冲击]]\n\n固定土地与人口反馈下，一次永久技术提升提高长期人口，稳态人均产出不变。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWith fixed land and feedback, a one-off technology improvement raises steady-state population, not income per person.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"6"},
		{"id":"pop56-004","type":"text","x":2080,"y":890,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[人口陷阱相图]]\n\n比较总收入与人口增长率；连续调整下 A、C 吸引，B 为分界，Y₃ 的峰值不是均衡。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCompare income and population growth. Under continuous adjustment A and C attract; B separates their basins.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"6"},
		{"id":"pop56-equilibrium-bridge","type":"text","x":40,"y":1220,"width":2480,"height":140,"text":"两种均衡条件：固定技术模型中人口净增长为零；课堂相图中总收入与人口增长率相等，可以共同正增长。离散更新的稳定性还须检查局部乘子。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe fixed-technology steady state has zero population growth; the classroom diagram equates income and population growth, possibly at positive rates. Discrete stability needs an additional local-multiplier check.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"pop56-031","type":"text","x":40,"y":1520,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[生育的工资与收入效应]]\n\n工资同时改变家庭资源和育儿时间成本；净生育效应取决于条件。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWages change both resources and the time cost of children; the net fertility response is conditional.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"2"},
		{"id":"pop56-030","type":"text","x":1060,"y":1520,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[生育数量质量权衡]]\n\n子女数量与每人教育投入通过交互成本相互制约。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe number of children and investment per child interact through their costs.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"2"},
		{"id":"pop56-032","type":"text","x":2080,"y":1520,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[教育回报与生育转型]]\n\n技术变迁若提高教育回报并推动质量投入，可以使生育下降。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nTechnological change may lower fertility if it raises education returns and shifts investment toward quality.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"2"},
		{"id":"pop56-choice-bridge","type":"text","x":40,"y":1850,"width":2480,"height":110,"text":"跨区桥：[[马尔萨斯技术冲击|一次技术提升]]固定后续技术和人口反馈；[[教育回报与生育转型|教育回报机制]]改变家庭选择条件，只是解释人口转型的一条有条件渠道。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA one-off technology shock holds later technology and demographic feedback fixed. Changing education returns alters family choices and offers one conditional route into demographic transition.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"pop56-014","type":"text","x":620,"y":2120,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[人口转型]]\n\n从高生育、高死亡向低生育、低死亡演变；常见先后次序不是普遍时间表。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA long-run shift from high fertility and mortality to low levels, not a universal timetable.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-015","type":"text","x":1500,"y":2120,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[人口惯性]]\n\n既有年龄结构会使人口在生育率下降后继续变化；出生总量还取决于各年龄女性人数。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nInherited age structure keeps shaping population after fertility changes; births also depend on women by age.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"5"},
		{"id":"pop56-016","type":"text","x":40,"y":2600,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[年龄抚养比]]\n\n儿童与老年人数相对劳动年龄人数的比率；年龄分组不是实际就业人数。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nChildren and older people relative to working-age people: an age proxy, not employment.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"4"},
		{"id":"pop56-017","type":"text","x":1060,"y":2600,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[人口红利]]\n\n有利的年龄结构变化创造增长机会，兑现仍需要健康、教育和有生产率的就业。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nFavorable age-structure changes create growth potential; health, education and productive jobs help realise it.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"4"},
		{"id":"pop56-018","type":"text","x":2080,"y":2600,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[年龄结构与人均产出]]\n\n人均产出 = 每名就业者产出 × 就业人口占比；劳动年龄占比上升本身不够。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOutput per person equals output per worker times the employment share. A larger working-age share alone is insufficient.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"4"},
		{"id":"pop56-window-bridge","type":"text","x":40,"y":2930,"width":2480,"height":110,"text":"跨区桥：[[人口转型|生育、死亡及队列变化]]重塑年龄结构。检查红利是否兑现，要打开[[人均GDP]]与[[劳动生产率]]；同一代人随后变老，年龄窗口也会移动。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nFertility, mortality and cohort changes reshape age structure. Assess realised gains through [[人均GDP|GDP per capita]] and [[劳动生产率|labour productivity]]; cohorts subsequently age.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"pop56-019","type":"text","x":40,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[人口老龄化]]\n\n人口年龄分布转向较高年龄；老年人口占比与老年抚养比的分母不同。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe population shifts toward older ages. The older-person share and old-age dependency ratio have different denominators.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"3"},
		{"id":"pop56-020","type":"text","x":1060,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[经济供养比]]\n\n按年龄劳动收入与消费剖面加权：有效生产者 ÷ 有效消费者。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nEffective producers divided by effective consumers, weighted by age-specific labour income and consumption.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"3"},
		{"id":"pop56-023","type":"text","x":2080,"y":3200,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[财政供养比]]\n\n按个人公共缴款与受益剖面加权：有效缴款者 ÷ 有效受益者。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nEffective contributors divided by beneficiaries, weighted by individual public-transfer outflows and inflows.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"3"},
		{"id":"pop56-021","type":"text","x":560,"y":3600,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[生命周期赤字]]\n\n当期消费 − 当期劳动收入；正缺口不能直接当作政府须支付的金额。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCurrent consumption minus labour income: a positive gap does not by itself establish the amount owed by government.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"3"},
		{"id":"pop56-022","type":"text","x":1560,"y":3600,"width":440,"height":300,"text":"## [[老年消费的筹资]]\n\n劳动收入、公共及私人净转移、资产收入减储蓄共同筹资。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nConsumption is financed by labour income, net public and private transfers, and asset income minus saving.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->","color":"3"},
		{"id":"pop56-support-comparison","type":"text","x":40,"y":3940,"width":2480,"height":320,"text":"### 三种比率回答三个问题\n\n[[年龄抚养比]]：非劳动年龄人数 ÷ 劳动年龄人数（常用年龄边界为 0–14、15–64、65+）。[[经济供养比]]：按劳动收入、消费权重计算的生产者 ÷ 消费者。[[财政供养比]]：按公共缴款、给付权重计算的缴款者 ÷ 受益者。后两者权重和考察范围不同，均不等于年龄抚养比的倒数。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAge dependency compares age-group headcounts; the economic support ratio weights labour income and consumption; the fiscal support ratio weights public contributions and benefits. The last two use different profiles and scopes, and neither is simply the reciprocal of age dependency.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n公共净转移是[[老年消费的筹资|筹资项]]之一；评价财政压力仍须核对缴款、受益、制度及固定年龄剖面的假设。\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPublic net transfers are one [[老年消费的筹资|financing component]]; fiscal assessment still requires contribution, benefit, institutional and age-profile assumptions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"pop56-edge-01","fromNode":"pop56-010","fromSide":"left","toNode":"pop56-011","toSide":"right","label":"出生事件标准化"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-02","fromNode":"pop56-010","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-012","toSide":"left","label":"死亡事件标准化"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-03","fromNode":"pop56-001","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-002","toSide":"left","label":"写明零增长阈值"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-04","fromNode":"pop56-002","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-003","toSide":"left","label":"给定阈值推稳态"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-05","fromNode":"pop56-003","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-004","toSide":"left","toEnd":"none","label":"均衡条件须区分"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-06","fromNode":"pop56-030","fromSide":"left","toNode":"pop56-031","toSide":"right","label":"工资冲击有两种效应"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-07","fromNode":"pop56-030","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-032","toSide":"left","label":"教育回报可推动质量投入"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-08","fromNode":"pop56-014","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-015","toSide":"left","label":"低生育后仍须看年龄结构"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-09","fromNode":"pop56-016","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-017","toSide":"left","label":"年龄窗口只提供机会"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-10","fromNode":"pop56-017","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-018","toSide":"left","label":"兑现须核就业与生产率"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-11","fromNode":"pop56-019","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-020","toSide":"left","label":"供养评价要加入经济剖面"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-12","fromNode":"pop56-020","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-023","toSide":"left","toEnd":"none","label":"经济活动 / 公共收支"},
		{"id":"pop56-edge-13","fromNode":"pop56-021","fromSide":"right","toNode":"pop56-022","toSide":"left","label":"缺口由转移及资产筹资"}
	]
}